 # Widget Animations
 
 ## Assets, groups and tracks
-A Widget Animation (WA_ asset) is a list of tracks, each in a Track Group; a group is one widget the animation moves (Target Widget; empty = the widget it plays on). Tracks start With Previous or After Previous plus Delay. Timing: Tween (Duration, Easing Linear / EaseIn / EaseOut / EaseInOut / Hold - the editor shows EaseInOut as "Cubic", Hold as "Constant", Custom as "Curve Asset" and a segment's Bezier as "Handles"; scripts keep the value names) or Spring (Spring: Duration and Bounce, or Stiffness / Damping / Mass - presets "@spring.Snappy", "@spring.Bouncy"...). A stagger (Expander) plays a track once per child, letter, word or line. A timeline is made as a Track Sheet (tracks, each from a start to an end) or a Dope Sheet (Key Mode): the same data, a Dope Sheet edited as keys only - each track is a row of keys, its start and end being its first and last key - and played with each row holding its first key's value until it gets there (a row of one key holds it throughout).
+A Widget Animation (WA_ asset) is a list of tracks, each in a Track Group; a group is one widget the animation moves (Target Widget; empty = the widget it plays on). Tracks start With Previous or After Previous plus Delay. Timing: Tween (Duration, Easing Linear / EaseIn / EaseOut / EaseInOut / Hold - the editor shows EaseInOut as "Cubic", Hold as "Constant", Custom as "Curve Asset" and a segment's Bezier as "Handles"; scripts keep the value names) or Spring (Spring: Duration and Bounce, or Stiffness / Damping / Mass - presets "@spring.Snappy", "@spring.Bouncy"...). A stagger (Expander) plays a track once per child, letter, word or line. A timeline is made as a Track Sheet (tracks, each from a start to an end) or a Dope Sheet (Key Mode): the same data, a Dope Sheet edited as keys only - each track is a row of keys, its start and end being its first and last key - and played with each row leaving its widget as authored until its first key, holding its last key after.
 
 ## Track types
 Fade (StartOpacity, EndOpacity), Scale (StartScale, EndScale, Overshoot), Slide (SlideFromDirection Up/Down/Left/Right, SlideDistance), Rotate (StartAngle, EndAngle), Pulse (PulseScaleAmount), Shake, Transform (keyframes of translation / scale / angle / shear, curved motion paths), MaterialScalar / MaterialVector (ScalarParameterName, StartScalarValue, EndScalarValue...), Shape (a shape's values over time), Design (brush, colors, fonts), cues (Sound, Event, Particles, Play Animation), and registered types (TypeParams).
